   "text": "The drawing matches tobramycin, and I wrote the SMILES from that identification and from memory of the PubChem isomeric SMILES. I did not rebuild each stereocentre from the wedges and hashes, so the stereodescriptors are the least certain part.\n\n- **Central ring:** a 2-deoxystreptamine cyclohexane carrying two NH2 groups, one OH and two glycosidic oxygens.\n- **Left ring:** a pyranose bearing CH2NH2, OH, a ring CH2, NH2 and the anomeric carbon. This is the 2,6-diamino-2,3,6-trideoxy sugar.\n- **Right ring:** a pyranose bearing the anomeric carbon, OH, NH2, OH and CH2OH. This is the 3-amino-3-deoxyglucose unit.\n\nSMILES: C1[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]1N)O[C@@H]2[C@@H](C[C@@H]([C@H](O2)CN)O)N)O)O[C@@H]3[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](O3)CO)O)N)O)N"
